---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Create a collection from an OpenAPI 3.0 or 3.1 document (a file or URL)

Usage: rustman import openapi [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>

Arguments:
  <SOURCE>
          The document: a file path or an http(s) URL, in JSON or YAML

Options:
      --into <DIR>
          Write the collection to this folder (default: the API title in kebab-case, in the workspace root); it must not exist or be empty

      --allow-remote-refs
          Fetch $refs to other http(s) documents instead of refusing them

      --sync
          Update an imported collection: merge the new document, keeping your edits, and move removed operations to _removed/

      --dry-run
          With --sync: print the change summary without writing any file

      --json
          With --sync: print the change summary as JSON

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
